  "transcript": "Think you know it all, five questions.  No Googling, no lifelines.  See how many you can get right  and drop your score in the comments when you are done.  Question one, and this one looks easy.  Which planet is known as the red planet?  The answer is Mars.  It looks red because of iron oxide,  basically rust, covering its surface.  Question two, what is the largest ocean on earth?  The Pacific Ocean, it covers more area  than all of earth's land put together.  Question three, how many sides does a hexagon have?  Six, a hexagon has six sides and six angles.  Think of a honeycomb cell.  Question four, what is the chemical symbol for gold?  The letters and you, the symbol comes from orum,  the Latin word for gold.  Question five, the last one.  In what year did humans first land on the moon?  1969, Apollo 11 landed on July 20th, 1969.  That is your score out of five.  Got all five, then you are officially smarter than the average internet.  Follow for round two.",
